    "This week is about the Psalms: the prayer book Jesus himself grew up praying. The first surprise is how blunt they are. David opens with: “How long, LORD? Will you forget me forever?” Four times he asks “how long”.",
    "Nobody tells him off for it. This complaint is in the Bible, which means honest frustration with God is a kind of prayer, not the opposite of one. If God feels far away right now, you can say exactly that.",
    "Then, without anything outside changing, the psalm turns: “But I trust in your loving kindness.” Trust here isn’t a feeling that arrived. It’s a choice David makes in the middle of the “how long”. You can make it too, even while the question is still open."
